{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00554","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00554@rel:R25-11#83415bd3","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00554","release":"R25-11","content":"function GetCurrentValueSize [SWS_PER_00554] Upstream: RS_PER_00017 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; std::uint64_t &gt; GetCurrentValueSize ( ara::core::StringView key) const noexcept; Returns the size (in bytes) of the value assigned to a key of this Key-Value Storage. GetCurrentValueSize may be delayed by an ongoing call from another thread to RemoveAllKeys or DiscardPendingChanges, or to SetValue, RemoveKey, RecoverKey, or ResetKey for the same key-value pair. This method uses transaction semantics, it sees the current state of transaction, not the actual physical storage. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/key_value_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::KeyValueStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kKeyNotFound rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td key td The key to look up. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt;std::uint64_t &gt; td A Result containing the size of the value in bytes. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Returned if the provided key does not exist in the Key-Value td Storage. td td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be read because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kValidationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the validity of stored data cannot be ensured. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00554","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"GetCurrentValueSize","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_KeyValueStorage_e55123.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-b045d30e3c97fa76","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":90,"rel":[],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"GetCurrentValueSize API in KeyValueStorage","n":16,"cap":"Figure 9.36: Interfaces for key-value-based data storage","sha":"b045d30e3c97fa76804aee0624930cbac3f6a04b3d15be2ecbb043d7043e46b6","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-67a0c9934f8b513a","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":55,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"KeyValueStorage GetCurrentValueSize method","n":14,"cap":"Figure 9.14: Interfaces required by State Management","sha":"67a0c9934f8b513aa4eccf85c17d21fac9083c5e1911afb304b3e862fabd997a","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-ac91624831463dd9","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_UpdateAndConfigurationManagement","p":18,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"GetCurrentValueSize method of KeyValueStorage","n":16,"cap":"Figure 5.2: Interfaces required by Update and Configuration Management from Functional Clusters Persistency and Time Synchronization","sha":"ac91624831